  "body": "Support 4th-axis and 5-axis NC simulation in `camcraft-gcode` and `crates/app` using machine kinematics.\n\n## Scope\n- Parse `A`/`B`/`C` rotary address words, `G93` inverse-time feeds (`feed_mm_min = move_length_mm * F`), and `G43.4`/`G49` RTCP mode.\n- Under RTCP (`G43.4`), map `X Y Z` tip coordinates and `A B C` words through `.mch` rotary axis vectors (`cl::pose`).\n- On non-RTCP machines (`controller.rtcp = false` from #1962), apply forward kinematics (`camcraft_post::kinematics`: `forward_part` / `forward_machine` from #2056) to transform machine coordinates into part-frame tip positions and `Move::axis` or `Move::rotary`.\n- Route posed and rotary moves through `FieldPlay` (`Stock::simulate_display`, `simulate_rotary_slice`) and `verify` (`solid_hits`, `bands_vs_fixtures_held`, `rapids_vs_fixtures_held`).\n- Report that the dexel column verdict does not judge tilted or rotary moves (`stock_sim::refuse_unjudged`).\n\nDepends on #2217, #2218, #2056, and #1962.\n\nDone means: Tests parse 4th-axis rotary/indexed and 5-axis RTCP/trunnion NC files into `Move::axis`/`Move::rotary`, run `FieldPlay` and posed `verify` checks, and report the column verdict limitation by name.\n\nPart of #2213\n",
